import json, os, urllib.request, pathlib
p=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
prompt="""You are GPT-6.2-Astra xhigh. Act as a CAD expert and industrial design visualization engineer. USER WANTS REAL PHYSICALLY MODELED CAD, NOT IMAGE GENERATION. The previous Blender images do NOT match the reference zeppelin lamp. Implement reference-match/build_match.py using CadQuery 2.8 Python 3.13 on Windows. We render CAD in Blender 5.3 later. DO NOT pretend exact match from a raster is proven.

Exact SOURCE IMAGE visual analysis (1536 x 864 pixels, black studio): SILVER LAMP BODY silhouette x=150..1378, top y=183, bottom y=512, width/body height=3.73. A STRAIGHT thin DARK steel double rail x=180..1366 at y_pixel=395. SILVER BASE centered at x745, base top y=676 bottom y=730, diameter about 421px (~one-third body length). Pedestal emerges from underside y=511, narrow waist x=658..826 at y=520..650 and flares gracefully into round base. ONE small round dimmer button at image x744 y623. Top silhouette rises from capsule point left x150 y392, scallops y300 at x250, y240 at x440, y187 at x625, two high lobes near x820 (y183) then descending to y235 at x1060, y320 at x1240, point x1378 y390. Lower lamella silhouette is about y395 at ends to y~512 centrally, ASYMMETRIC: height ABOVE rail is 212px, BELOW ~117px. There are about NINE scale-like smooth satin silver CURVED SCOOP lobes, concave metallic faces with dark-to-light reflections. Only ONE little circular pivot cap per station along the rail, NOT a row of 3 dots per paddle. Warm ivory-yellow gentle glow behind each lower scoop and gaps. The past CAD was nine near-vertical FAT symmetrical paper-like paddles, no match. Material must be beautiful brushed satin silver with smooth specular gradients, slim rail, continuous shell taper and warm bottom, black background. Must be actually modeled not painted.

Physical target: body length 380 mm, rail Z=102mm, overall height approx 167mm, upper shell reaches z=167, lower z=62. FOOT diameter 130mm, height 13mm, curved hourglass pedestal from z=13..65. Pivot x coordinates approx [-166,-124,-82,-41,0,41,82,124,166]mm at z=102. Each leaf's TOP reaches pivot_z + [20,33,47,58,65,58,47,33,20]mm, BOTTOM pivot_z - [16,25,32,37,40,37,32,25,16]mm. Typical halfwidth in X [25,37,47,51,57,51,47,37,25]mm. Need smooth overlapped elliptical SCALLOPED edges, curved in depth like architectural metallic louvers, not flat ellipses or paper shapes. Reference camera is front elevation facing +Y from near y negative, slightly above base.

CAD geometry: build each lamella from smooth sheet surfaces: per local X coordinate x between [-w,w], top Z = top_i * sqrt(1 - (x/w)^2), bottom Z=-bottom_i *sqrt(...); Y depth is CYLINDRICAL bend function of x only so DEVELOPABLE (e.g. Y = Y_layer + 9 to 14mm quadratic/circular sag across width). Loft at maybe 33-49 cross sections, sheet thickness 0.6mm normal to surface, with rounded very tips and smooth curvature. Central panel should show curve and bright rolled perimeter. Overlap neighboring stations like metallic scales. Make one front visible paddle per station, plus optional back complementary skin, but avoid two visually competing rows. Use depth lanes 14-18mm pitch with enough running clearance; note cam 0deg front sees front y negative, more negative surfaces occlude rear ones. Need mechanical plausibility: shafts along Y axis through pivot at each station, modular small clamp behind sheet; black/steel structural rod along X just above centerline, 9 tiny round hinge caps above panel faces along axis; hidden module-1 20-tooth rack/pinion if feasible but don't claim verified contact without checks. One DOF shared across nine stations, at least shape can rotate +/-10deg without apparent collisions. At reference pose leaf angle theta=0°, other pose theta=20° for proof of concept. Face still silver no unnecessary bosses. Knob on pedestal can be simple fixed dimmer. Fixed warm luminous opal diffuser mounted behind the lower portion of shells, physically part of CAD, glowing in Blender without fake band. For real light material label 'light'. No loose parts in air: connect pedestal to rail and base.

OUTPUT code only: a SINGLE executable reference-match/build_match.py. Use CadQuery API correctly. Build several CAD solids, export assembly_reference.step and assembly_open.step, individual key parts STEP if possible, and scene.json EXACT JSON schema compatible with existing parent's tested Blender procedural import:
{"models":{part_name:{"v":[flat x,y,z mm], "f":[flat triangle indices]}},"parts":[{"g":part_type,"motion":"fixed"|"leaf"|"gear"|"rack","name":unique,"p":[x,y,z],"color":"matte"|"frame"|"metal"|"light"}],"kinematics":{"closed_deg":0,"open_deg":20,"rack_pitch_radius_mm":10}}.
Moving leaf mesh vertices must be LOCAL relative to each pivot at origin, with each instance p=[pivot_x,0,pivot_z], and rotate around Y axis; fixed vertices in WORLD with p=[0,0,0]. Tessellate solid cad geometry to triangles and store flat arrays using cq tessellate. Need place components and colors accurately, and call assembly.save for STEP on CadQuery Assembly, ensure valid solids, print bounds, and never report complete fabrication-ready if not. Add a check that body x width 370-410mm, body z top 160-170, body z bottom 60-70, round base diameter ~130. Simple source code, no comments or docstrings. Most importantly actual 3D CAD geometries should LOOK AS CLOSE AS POSSIBLE to reference picture.
Return ONLY source Python code, no fences, no explanation."""
body={"model":"gpt-6.2-astra","reasoning":{"effort":"xhigh"},"max_output_tokens":17000,"input":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":prompt}]}]}
req=urllib.request.Request("https://api.openai.com/v1/responses",data=json.dumps(body).encode(),headers={"Authorization":"Bearer "+os.environ["OPENAI_API_KEY"],"Content-Type":"application/json"},method="POST")
try:
 with urllib.request.urlopen(req,timeout=350) as resp: data=json.load(resp)
 out="\n".join(c.get("text","") for row in data.get("output",[]) for c in row.get("content",[]) if c.get("type")=="output_text")
 if out.lstrip().startswith(chr(96)*3):out=out.strip().split("\n",1)[1].rsplit(chr(96)*3,1)[0]
 (p/"build_match.py").write_text(out,encoding="utf-8")
 (p/"api_usage.json").write_text(json.dumps({"model":data.get("model"),"status":data.get("status"),"usage":data.get("usage")},indent=2),encoding="utf-8")
 print(json.dumps({"model":data.get("model"),"status":data.get("status"),"length":len(out),"tokens":data.get("usage",{}).get("total_tokens"),"leading":out[:140]},ensure_ascii=True),flush=True)
except urllib.error.HTTPError as ex: print("HTTP",ex.code,ex.read(1000).decode(errors="replace"),flush=True)
except Exception as e:print("ERROR",type(e).__name__,str(e)[:500],flush=True)
